  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000120900,
      "SummaryText": "The North Platte Sustainable Beef facility is a beef processing plant located on the east side of North Platte, Nebraska. The facility will employ approximately 850 Team Members and includes an ammonia refrigeration system integral to its operations. The refrigeration system contains approximately 80,000 pounds of anhydrous ammonia, which is classified as a regulated substance under 40 CFR Part 68 due to its toxicity and potential off-site consequences in the event of a release.\n\nSustainable Beef is committed to operating safely, protecting our Team Members, the surrounding community, and the environment. We have developed and implemented a comprehensive Process Safety Management (PSM) program and Risk Management Plan (RMP) to prevent accidental releases of ammonia. Our policies emphasize preventive maintenance, training, and hazard identification as key strategies for minimizing risk.\n\nAt the time of this submission, the facility has no history of accidental releases involving anhydrous ammonia that resulted in on-site injuries, off-site impacts, or environmental harm.\n\nOur emergency response program has been coordinated with local emergency services and includes notification procedures, training, and drills to ensure readiness in the event of an ammonia release. We plan to continue working closely with the Local Emergency Planning Committee (LEPC) to align on emergency response strategies.\n\nAs part of our ongoing commitment to safety, Sustainable Beef continuously evaluates and improves its refrigeration system, training programs, and process controls. Planned improvements include continued emergency response training, and process hazard analysis updates as the facility ramps up operations."
    }
